# Aether Interface Architecture (.clinerules)

## 0. Strict Git & Repository Invariant (ZERO TOLERANCE)
- NEVER run any `git` commands under any circumstances (zero `git add`, `commit`, `push`, `diff`, `checkout`, `stash`, etc.).
- Version control is strictly reserved for the human developer.
- Confine all actions strictly to reading files, surgical editing, and running targeted test/verification scripts.

## 1. Linear Execution Protocol (Read -> Code -> Sync Docs)
Execute every task in this exact three-phase order:
1. **READ FIRST:** Thoroughly inspect `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/SYSTEM_MAP.md` at the start of every task. Never guess architectural boundaries, data contracts, or component roles.
2. **EXECUTE CODE:** Apply surgical, minimal diffs. Zero unsolicited refactoring or out-of-scope edits. Delete replaced or superseded code immediately (zero zombie code).
3. **SYNC DOCS LAST:** Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/SYSTEM_MAP.md` precisely once at the very end of the task if boundaries, files, models, or IPC contracts were introduced or altered. Never loop between writing code and editing docs mid-task.

## 2. Test Integrity & Verification Standards (Zero Cheating)
- **Fix the Software, Not the Test:** Never weaken, bypass, relax, or mock out a failing assertion just to achieve a green test pass. If a test fails, diagnose and fix the underlying runtime defect.
- **Full Transparency:** Always report the complete test output—including skipped, warned, or failing tests. Never omit or obscure failures.
- **Deterministic & Lean:**
  - Zero wall-clock sleeps (`time.sleep()`, arbitrary `QTest.qWait()`); use deterministic condition polling (`qtbot.waitUntil`).
  - Do NOT generate redundant test files or test bloat for minor tweaks or visual polish.